.TH DAQ_ENV_TOOLS.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
daq_env_tools.py \- dump the process environment to JSON, or load one into the script's own process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 daq_env_tools.py
.RB [ \-c | \-\-capture ]
.RB [ \-r | \-\-restore ]
.RB [ \-o | \-\-output
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-i | \-\-input
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-f | \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-e | \-\-exec
.IR CMD ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Always prints the input and output file names first.
.TP
.B \-\-capture
prints every environment variable as
.I KEY: value
on stdout and writes the whole environment as JSON to the output file.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
reads the input JSON into
.B os.environ
of this Python process and exits.
A child process cannot change its parent's environment, so the calling
shell is unaffected: from the command line
.B \-\-restore
has no effect.
.PP
The module also defines
.BR store_restore_exec_command (),
which swaps the environment around one shell command; nothing calls it,
and
.B \-\-exec
does not reach it.
.PP
.B Secrets.
.B \-\-capture
copies every variable verbatim, including tokens and credential paths
(for example
.BR GH_TOKEN ,
.BR VAULT_TOKEN ,
.BR KRB5CCNAME ),
to stdout and to a file created with the process umask, normally
world\-readable.
Do not run it in a shell that holds credentials, or pipe its output to a
log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-capture
as above; refuses to overwrite an existing output file without
.BR \-f .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-restore
as above; exits 1 if the input file does not exist.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-output " FILE
default
.IR default_env_out.json .
.TP
.BI \-i " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-input " FILE
default
.IR default_env_in.json .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
allow overwriting the output file.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-d ", " \-s ", " \-\-config ", " \-e
accepted and ignored.
.SH FILES
.IR default_env_out.json ,
.I default_env_in.json
in the working directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 when the output exists without
.BR \-f ,
or the input is missing for
.BR \-r ;
2 for a command\-line error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
python3 daq_env_tools.py \-c \-o muse\-env.json
chmod 600 muse\-env.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR env (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
